From: kierandrewett <kieran@drewett.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] Route diagnostic input before window and Wayland dispatch

Stage captured-event is downstream of Mutter's Clutter event filter. A
Wayland pointer with a focused surface consumes motion and buttons in that
filter, so the non-reactive recovery overlay never sees them. Dispatch its
private callback after the existing embargoes, physical seat update and
keybindings, before window click handling or Wayland delivery. The plugin
keeps panel hit testing and press ownership; no focus or Lua policy changes.

diff --git a/src/core/events.c b/src/core/events.c
--- a/src/core/events.c
+++ b/src/core/events.c
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
 #include "backends/meta-idle-manager.h"
 #include "compositor/compositor-private.h"
 #include "compositor/meta-window-actor-private.h"
+#include "compositor/plugins/gnoblin-plugin-input.h"
 #include "core/display-private.h"
 #include "core/gnoblin-native-control.h"
 #include "core/window-private.h"
@@ -358,6 +359,12 @@ meta_display_handle_event (MetaDisplay        *display,
   if (stage_has_grab (display))
     return CLUTTER_EVENT_PROPAGATE;
 
+  /* Actor captured-event runs only after this filter. Wayland pointer
+   * delivery can consume the event before that signal, even when the
+   * diagnostic overlay is painted above the focused client surface. */
+  if (gnoblin_plugin_input_handle_event (G_OBJECT (display), event))
+    return CLUTTER_EVENT_STOP;
+
   if (window)
     {
       if (meta_window_handle_ungrabbed_event (window, event))
